Sony Alpha trigger (camera_trigger_capture, PTP_OC_SONY_SDIO_ControlDevice branch) pressed like a finger: half-press,
WAIT for focus (AFStatus 0xC223 = 2 or 0xD213 in {2,3} read at least 100 ms after the press; at most 2000 ms; manual
focus = 100 ms), full-press, HOLD it until the camera registers the shot (0xD215 >= 0x8000, or ObjectAdded 0xC201 /
CapturedEvent 0xC206; at least 150 ms, at most 1000 ms), then release S2 and S1. Every event that is not an AF one is
put back in the queue, in order, for camera_wait_for_event. Log lines "sony trigger: ..." with the timings.
Why: upstream (2.5.34 and master) presses S2 23 ms after S1 and releases as soon as 0xD213 reads 2 — measured on an
ILCE-1 (Prism, 30/09-01/10/2026, PTP through ImageCaptureCore): 0xD213 = 2 after 43 ms was the stale value of the
previous lock, release at 66 ms, the AFStatus events (1 x4, then 2) arrived AFTER the release and the body did not
shoot (0xD215 stayed 0 for 30 s; one shot in ten). The FX30 shot only because its AF is faster.
Remove when libgphoto2 upstream changes this sequence.
